Note: This is my first ever Usenet post - I think it's fitting that
it's a YAFAP!

I discovered nethack about 5 years ago and I dropped it quickly
because it was just Too Hard(tm). But I couldn't resist the temptation
and I've played on and off until about a year ago when I decided that
I was going to finish it. I just did ;-)

My favourite class is the Archeologist but I've gotten further with
Samurai and Valkyrie. So I tend to cycle between them - the Valkyrie
won! I think the most important factor was learning from a string of
YASD - don't try on rings in a temple (conflict ruined my most
promising Archeologist), don't underestimate the damage them floating
eyes can do and don't assume you're wearing your amulet of reflection
- wands of death after a nymph visit are particularly cruel.

A wand of wishing on the second level was the crucial factor - it
produced the vital Speed boots, Cloak of magic Resistance, Silver
dragon scale mail, gauntlets of power and bag of holding that would be
with me throughout the entire game (I can't overstate how cool SDSM
and Magic Resistance are!!). From thereon the first third of the game
passed uneventfully. The mines were easier than ever and I didn't
bother with Sokoban.

The Valkyrie quest is ridicously easy once you have a ring of
levitation and Excalibur at +5. In fact it's the only quest I've ever
finished (3 times now). The castle went by uneventfully until - I got
the second wand of wishing. This brought a succession of stupid
mistakes - I wished for the standard scrolls of charging (having lost
my first one whilst having an underwater spat with a few eels, sharks
and piranha) and then for a magic marker. All good and well. I then
confused myself to rustproof my armour (iron helm) and accidently
wasted my scrolls of charging when I forgot to unconfuse myself! I
then panicked and zapped the wand of wishing for more scrolls and
ended up hitting 'enter' too quickly and wasting the last wish! (4
potential wishes wasted! Kids - don't try this at home!).

It got better - I then decided to try and polypile for scrolls of
charging and ended up converting an unspecified wand into
cancellation... You can guess what happened from there - Bag of
Holding + vital stash (including wand of wishing) went up in smoke...

By then I had an AC of -33 and I decided that I was just going to go
on anyway. It was my first time in Gehennom so I proceeded cautiously.
I was surprised at how easily Asmodeus, Jubilex and Orcus went down (I
don't remember seeing Baalzebub) which gave me hope that I was going
to make it through. I visited Vlad and discovered that I no longer had
7 candles... This combined with an encounter with a master mindflayer
introduced the most boring section of the game - backtracking to
minetown to get more candles and redoing all the mazes I had
supposedly already done.

The most exciting section was finding the vibrating square and duking
it out with Rodney. I was lucky to have three amulets of lifesaving
and Rodney used up two on my ascension run. I can't quite describe how
frantic this is! For a turn based game the level of tension is simply
unbelievable... Rodney appeared 10 times in all (and cast double
trouble twice so I ended up killing him 14 times) and is the biggest
pain in the neck I've yet experienced in a lifetime of playing
computer games. (I had a few wands of death and they helped
considerably but I just didn't have enough charges and I had to go
mano a mano more times than was comfortable)

I had a ring of conflict on permanently through the planes and I think
that made the difference - it certainly helped with the air
elementals. The astral plane was a nightmare but, continuing the theme
of good luck, the first altar I found was Tyr's! Battle scarred and
bruised and with far fewer possessions than I expected to have but
with body intact -

